{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>There is — also</b>: both are joined. The meaning: there is a straight way set before a man, and it is the way of the commandments, and after the way is set before him and he turns aside from it, he will find the ways of death." "And the word 'also' — to include abandonment of the straight way. And likewise the meaning: also because the desire of the world and its pleasures pains the heart of him who occupies himself with them, for HaShem pains him, and the end of the joy of pleasures brings him grief."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:42.677100854Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}